From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aayush Misra <aayushm@amd.com>
Date: Sun, 17 Aug 2026 19:06:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] sim: microblaze: do not alias SLR/SHR onto the PC

The simulator models only two special registers (PC and MSR) and selects
between them with "CPU.spregs[IMM & 0x1]".  MicroBlaze's stack protection
registers SLR (SPR 0x0800) and SHR (SPR 0x0802) both have bit 0 clear, so
"mts rslr, rN" wrote straight into spregs[0] - the program counter.

GCC's libgcc/config/microblaze/crti.S initialises SLR/SHR in __init, so
every newlib program built with this toolchain reset its own PC to 0 and
span forever in the startup code.  Reproducer:

        addik   r11, r0, 0
        mts     rslr, r11
        addi    r3, r0, 9
        bri     0

Route any SPR other than PC/MSR to a catch-all slot instead.

The interp.c hunk revives the existing but unreachable "tracing" code (the
variable was never assigned) behind the MB_SIM_TRACE environment variable,
which prints PC and opcode per instruction.

Without this patch the toolchain still builds, but nothing can be run under
the simulator, so the testsuite is meaningless.  Not submitted upstream.

Signed-off-by: Aayush Misra <aayushm@amd.com>

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 sim/microblaze/interp.c         | 3 +++
 sim/microblaze/microblaze-sim.h | 2 +-
 sim/microblaze/microblaze.h     | 7 ++++++-
 3 files changed, 10 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/sim/microblaze/microblaze.h
+++ b/sim/microblaze/microblaze.h
@@ -31,7 +31,12 @@
 #define RB      CPU.regs[rb]
 /* #define IMM     immword */
 
-#define SA	CPU.spregs[IMM & 0x1]
+/* Only PC (SPR 0x0000) and MSR (SPR 0x0001) are modelled.  Every other
+   special register, notably SLR (0x0800) and SHR (0x0802) which crti.S
+   initialises, must land in the catch-all slot: masking the SPR number
+   with 0x1 would alias them onto spregs[0], i.e. the PC.  */
+#define SPRNUM	(IMM & 0x3FFF)
+#define SA	CPU.spregs[SPRNUM > 1 ? 2 : SPRNUM]
 
 #define IMM_H	CPU.imm_high
 #define IMM_L	((inst & IMM_MASK) >> IMM_LOW)
--- a/sim/microblaze/microblaze-sim.h
+++ b/sim/microblaze/microblaze-sim.h
@@ -34,7 +34,7 @@
  struct microblaze_regset
 {
   signed_4	regs[32];		/* primary registers */
-  signed_4	spregs[2];		/* pc + msr */
+  signed_4	spregs[3];		/* pc + msr + catch-all for unmodelled */
   int		cycles;
   int		insts;
   unsigned_1	imm_enable;
--- a/sim/microblaze/interp.c
+++ b/sim/microblaze/interp.c
@@ -111,6 +111,7 @@
 }
 
 static int tracing = 0;
+#define TRACING_INIT() (tracing = (getenv ("MB_SIM_TRACE") != NULL))
 
 void
 sim_engine_run (SIM_DESC sd,
@@ -137,6 +138,8 @@
   bonus_cycles = 0;
   insts = 0;
 
+  TRACING_INIT ();
+
   while (1)
     {
       /* Fetch the initial instructions that we'll decode. */
